---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BrandLogo from '../components/BrandLogo.astro';
const home = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Dictate"
  description="How Dictate processes speech, stores local data, and uses network access on Mac and Windows."
>
  <main class="policy-page">
    <header>
      <a class="wordmark" href={home}><BrandLogo size={30}/><span>Dictate</span></a>
      <a class="back" href={home}>Back to home</a>
    </header>

    <article>
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy · September 11, 2026</p>
      <h1>Your voice<br/><em>stays yours.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Dictate processes speech on your computer. It has no account, advertising, analytics, transcript upload, or paid transcription service.</p>

      <section>
        <h2>What stays on your computer</h2>
        <p>Live microphone samples exist in memory only while you record and transcribe. Dictate does not save raw microphone audio to a file.</p>
        <p>Your preferences, dictionary, optional history, downloaded models, and any transcript waiting for recovery are stored in your local application-data folder. Recovery contains text, never audio.</p>
        <div class="platform-grid">
          <div><strong>Mac</strong><span><code>~/Library/Application Support/Dictate/</code></span></div>
          <div><strong>Windows</strong><span><code>%APPDATA%\app.dictate.portable\</code></span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>When Dictate uses the internet</h2>
        <p>Dictation and dictionary correction run locally after your selected model is installed. An internet connection is used only to download speech-model assets during setup.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Apple Speech may ask macOS to install an Apple-managed speech asset.</li>
          <li>NVIDIA Parakeet and Whisper assets come from their public model repositories on Hugging Face.</li>
          <li>Windows verifies downloaded model files against pinned SHA-256 checksums before loading them.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Permissions and text insertion</h2>
        <p>Microphone access is required to record. On Mac, optional Accessibility access lets Dictate insert text into other apps. On Windows, Dictate uses the focused editable field and Unicode input. If insertion cannot finish, the transcript remains inside Dictate so you can copy or retry it.</p>
        <p>Explicitly choosing Copy replaces your clipboard contents. Automatic Windows insertion preserves the clipboard. Some Mac editors require temporary pasteboard delivery; Dictate restores the earlier pasteboard when another app has not changed it in the meantime.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>History and diagnostics</h2>
        <p>History is optional and its retention is under your control. Turning history off affects future dictations; deleting history removes the entries already stored on that computer.</p>
        <p>Operational logs may contain app identifiers, accessibility roles, state changes, and character counts. They are designed not to contain transcript text, dictionary contents, microphone audio, or clipboard contents.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="source-note">
        <h2>Open for inspection</h2>
        <p>This policy describes the current open-source build. You can inspect the implementation, third-party notices, and release validation in the repository.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/leviackerman05/dictate/blob/main/PRIVACY.md">Policy source ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/leviackerman05/dictate/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md">Third-party notices ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/leviackerman05/dictate">Source code ↗</a></div>
      </section>
    </article>

    <footer><span>Dictate · MIT licensed</span><a href={`${home.replace(/\/$/, '')}/download`}>Download Dictate</a></footer>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy-page{max-width:980px;margin:auto;padding:0 40px}header,footer{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:30px 0}.wordmark{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-size:21px;font-weight:650}.back,footer{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}article{padding:58px 0 48px}.eyebrow{margin:0 0 18px;color:var(--action);font-size:12px;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}h1{margin:0;font-size:clamp(50px,8vw,82px);font-weight:600;line-height:.98;letter-spacing:-.045em}h1 em{color:var(--action);font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:400}.lede{max-width:720px;margin:28px 0 70px;color:var(--muted);font-size:21px;line-height:1.6}section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(190px,280px) minmax(0,1fr);column-gap:50px;padding:34px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}section h2{grid-row:1 / span 6;margin:0;font-size:22px;letter-spacing:-.025em}section p,section ul,.platform-grid,.links{grid-column:2;margin:0 0 17px;color:var(--muted);font-size:15px;line-height:1.7}section ul{padding-left:20px}.platform-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px}.platform-grid div{display:grid;gap:8px;padding:16px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;background:var(--surface)}.platform-grid strong{color:var(--text)}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:12px}.source-note{margin-top:20px;padding:34px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px}.links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px;margin-bottom:0}.links a,footer a{color:var(--action);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:700px){.policy-page{padding:0 22px}article{padding-top:34px}.lede{margin-bottom:48px;font-size:18px}section{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:14px}section h2{grid-row:auto}section p,section ul,.platform-grid,.links{grid-column:1}.platform-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.source-note{padding:24px 20px}footer{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}}
</style>
